/// `ViT.forward` then `Aligner.forward`: a patch grid to one language-width row per
/// aligner cell, and the spelling of the token that addresses an image span.
///
/// The existing `DeepSeekV41VisionForwardTests` fixture came from an independent
/// numpy mirror of `inference/vision.py`, which pins the port against a SECOND
/// transcription of the rule. These vectors come from the reference module itself,
/// which is what the gate asks for.
///
/// The fixture is chosen to fail loudly: two heads make the shared 2D rotary a real
/// frequency vector rather than a no-op, three patch columns are ODD so the aligner
/// pads to four (a port that crops instead of padding drops a column and produces a
/// cell), and a downsample ratio of two splits the aligner into two cells.
